feat(scheduler): Slice 5 — Distill SystemJob (L1->L2 roll-up, zero model calls)

The scheduler + vault-memory convergence, the last core scheduler slice.

- memory.rs distill(): deterministic nightly roll-up. Reads the last N days
  of L1 daily notes (Daily/YYYY-MM-DD.md), strips frontmatter/headings/bullet
  markers, and runs each line through the SAME salience extractor +
  novelty-gated remember() that auto_capture uses. Durable facts promote to L2
  atoms; repeats reinforce, never duplicate. Idempotent-ish (re-run = mostly
  reinforce) so coalesce-on-resume catches a backlog safely. ZERO model calls —
  pure code + local embeddings, free to run nightly.
- scheduler.rs: fire_one now returns FireOutcome (Enqueued|Skipped|SystemJob).
  SystemJob is logged 'running' in the txn, then EXECUTED ASYNC after commit
  (embeddings can't run in the writer closure). run_system_job dispatches by
  name (distill|reconcile) and back-writes ok/error + snippet into schedule_run.
  run_distill resolves the vault + Memory dir THROUGH THE JAIL BROKER, uses the
  in-process embedder. Ticker + run_now both handle the async job path.
- lib.rs: scheduler_run_now is now async (app+broker+drain state).

Now a 'Nightly memory distill' schedule (already in the UI's job dropdown)
actually runs the roll-up. Scheduler + memory, working together.
First compile of distill + FireOutcome refactor — flag if cargo throws.
